📊 Query Breakdown

Query 4 — Colleague NPS

SEL * FROM rxcoe_sa.PK_Automation_Colleague_NPS;

Purpose:
Retrieves all records from the PK_Automation_Colleague_NPS table to analyze Net Promoter Score (NPS) data related to colleagues, providing a baseline sentiment score.

⸻

Query 1 — Wecare Call Center KPIs

This complex query joins the Wecare call center performance table with abandonment metrics derived from daily call activity data.

Key Metrics Calculated:
	•	Abandonment Rate:
Using numerator (TOT_ABNDN_CALL_CNT + TOT_HOLD_ABNDN_CALL_CNT)
and denominator (TOT_NON_DRV_UP_CALL_CNT).
	•	Average Handle Times:
Includes time to answer, calls on hold, and hold time metrics.
	•	Filters Applied:
	•	Only retail stores (AREA_NBR IN (2,4,8,12,14,16))
	•	Excludes CarePlus stores
	•	Active stores only (CLOS_DT IS NULL)
	•	Fiscal week ≥ 202201

This data helps evaluate call handling efficiency and customer experience at the store level.

⸻

Query (Main Automation Metrics) — Store Script Utilization

This query measures automation utilization in pharmacy operations by analyzing prescription fill records.

Key Outputs:
	•	Total Scripts vs. Automated Scripts
	•	Automation Type (Y/N)
	•	Robot Type: SP 100, SP 200, KL, CRS, Parata, etc.
	•	Number of Cells per Robot

Business Purpose:
Identifies how effectively automation robots are used in each store, linking fill processes to robot deployments to calculate utilization rates and operational efficiency.

